"""Editorial question designs for toys, collecting, and scale models."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


TOYS = """history_origins|A Toy in Its Childhood Context|Which dated social or manufacturing change shaped a named toy?|Use catalog, patent, object, and family records.
famous_examples|A Toy's Actual Play|How did children use a named toy beyond its advertised purpose?|Compare product design with consented observation or oral history.
hidden_stories|Makers and Players behind a Toy|Whose labor and play experiences are absent from its brand story?|Use manufacturing and family evidence.
beginner_explainers|Toy, Child, and Setting|What makes a toy suitable for a particular child and play context?|Check current age guidance, abilities, interest, and actual components.
advanced_concepts|Open-Ended Play Claims|Does a toy permit multiple child-led uses and what evidence supports learning claims?|Use bounded observations, not developmental promises.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Unverified Toy Origin|Which early design or manufacturer claim can be dated?|Compare patents, catalogs, packaging, and surviving examples.
technology_innovation|Electronics in a Toy|Which play action changed when a toy gained sensors or software?|Test released version and data/privacy requirements.
people_personalities|A Toy Designer's Revision|What documented feedback altered shape, materials, or interaction?|Use prototypes, test records, and attributed accounts.
major_events|A Toy Recall|What defect and affected production dates did an official notice identify?|Use current regulator notice and product identifiers.
how_it_works|From Concept to Plaything|How do design, prototype, age determination, testing, and sale connect?|Trace a real product and jurisdiction.
rise_fall|A Toy Leaves Shelves|Was a product withdrawn for safety, demand, or licensing?|Separate documented reasons from collector lore.
then_vs_now|One Toy across Versions|Which size, material, or rules changed over time?|Compare identified production runs and labeling.
future_developments|A Proposed Connected Toy|Which safety, privacy, and repair questions remain?|Treat concept claims as unverified until tested.
myths_vs_facts|Educational on the Box?|What learning outcome was measured, for which children and conditions?|Examine original study and marketing language separately.
documentary_stories|A Toy's Design Trail|How did prototype, test, and production change a play object?|Follow dated artifacts and credited makers.
creative_brief|The Intended Play Experience|What child age and interaction did a design brief specify?|Compare brief, actual product, and observed play.
materials_and_tools|What a Toy Is Made Of|Which material and component choices affect use and durability?|Use product and test data for the specified version.
process_breakdown|Testing a Toy Prototype|What did playtesting and safety assessment reveal?|Separate observation, compliance test, and design response.
composition_choice|Shapes Invite Play|How do size, color, and moving parts cue an action?|Observe a bounded child group with consent.
collaborative_authorship|Many Makers of a Toy|Who designed play, mechanism, artwork, packaging, and testing?|Check credits and product records.
adaptation_across_media|A Character Becomes a Toy|Which story traits survive as physical play features?|Compare source, license, and released object.
audience_reception|Children and Caregivers Respond|What do different users actually do or report?|Use age-specific, consented evidence with sampling limits.
cultural_context|A Toy in a Household|How do space, language, and family routines affect its use?|Ask families rather than assume one play norm.
preservation_restoration|Saving a Play Object|Which wear, missing parts, or battery damage affects interpretation?|Use museum condition and provenance records.
rights_and_attribution|Toy Design and Character Rights|Which maker or license covers form and story?|Check patents, trademarks, and agreements as applicable.
style_comparison|Two Toys for One Play Goal|How do rules and affordances differ for similarly aged users?|Compare actual products and observed play.
creative_failure|A Toy Redesigned|What documented test or recall led to change?|Use official notices and version evidence.
field_age_appropriate_design|Intended Age and Actual Parts|Do product features and labeling suit the stated age?|Check current official age guidance and test records.
field_caregiver_choices|Selecting for One Child|Which interest, ability, environment, and supervision matter?|Use caregiver judgment with current safety information.
field_play_and_learning|What Play Reveals|Which skills are practiced in observed play, and which claims remain untested?|Separate behavior from long-term learning outcomes.
field_household_routines|Toy in Daily Life|Where is it stored, used, cleaned, and shared?|Use household accounts and actual use.
field_child_safety|A Toy's Safety Record|Which small-part, material, battery, or recall information applies?|Verify current product and jurisdiction; avoid certifying safety from appearance.
"""

COLLECTING = """history_origins|A Toy Collecting Community|Which dated catalog, club, or market shaped a specific collecting practice?|Use records and avoid a single origin.
famous_examples|A Collection with Provenance|What can a named toy collection document about production and play?|Inspect accession records, object dates, and use traces.
hidden_stories|Collectors beyond the Price Guide|Whose repair, cataloging, and sharing labor preserves toys?|Use credited collection records and oral histories.
beginner_explainers|Identify a Toy Version|Which maker, date, material, and marking distinguish variants?|Compare original packaging and catalog evidence.
advanced_concepts|Condition versus Originality|How do repairs and replacement parts affect historical interpretation?|Document intervention and evidence, not investment advice.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Toy with Unclear Provenance|Which ownership or manufacture link is missing?|Trace records and mark uncertainty rather than invent a story.
technology_innovation|Digital Collection Catalogs|Does a database improve identification and access?|Compare metadata quality, privacy, and upkeep.
people_personalities|A Collector's Criteria|Why did a named collector assemble a specific set?|Use attributed interviews and accession notes.
major_events|A Collection Donated|What changed in preservation and public access after a transfer?|Read donor, accession, and exhibit records.
how_it_works|Cataloging a Toy Collection|How are identification, condition, provenance, and storage recorded?|Follow a real catalog entry and limitations.
rise_fall|A Collecting Market Shifts|Which documented supply or demand change altered interest?|Use dated sales and avoid price forecasts.
then_vs_now|A Toy after Decades|Which wear, repair, or packaging change affects interpretation?|Compare condition reports and photographs.
future_developments|A Collection's Long-Term Plan|What space, catalog, and succession decisions remain?|Treat proposals as conditional.
myths_vs_facts|Rare Means Valuable?|How do condition, provenance, demand, and sale terms alter a price claim?|Use dated transactions; no investment recommendation.
documentary_stories|One Toy's Ownership Trail|How did it move from playroom to collection?|Trace documented transfers and gaps.
lived_experience|Living with a Collection|What enjoyment and work does collecting add to daily life?|Use consented collector accounts and logs.
institutional_pathway|Museum Acquisition|Which criteria and paperwork govern accepting a toy collection?|Read actual museum policy and donor agreement.
incentives_norms|Why Collect This Toy?|How do memory, scholarship, completion, and market signals differ?|Ask collectors; avoid assuming profit motive.
access_and_exclusion|Who Can Participate?|Which price, space, language, and access barriers shape collecting?|Use situated accounts and market data.
community_variation|Different Collecting Traditions|How do local clubs and online groups value condition or play history?|Compare stated norms without a single standard.
policy_in_practice|A Collection's Use Rules|How do handling or lending policies affect actual access?|Compare written policy and practice.
survey_vs_story|A Market Trend Claim|Do online listings represent completed sales or collector interests?|Check sample and transaction evidence.
power_and_voice|Whose Collection Story Is Told?|Who decides whether an object is valued for play, rarity, or design?|Compare curator, donor, and user perspectives.
unintended_consequence|Keeping Everything|What storage, household, and conservation burdens accumulate?|Measure costs and space without judgment.
comparative_setting|Toy at Home and Museum|How do handling and interpretation differ by setting?|Compare same object or matched examples.
change_over_time|A Collection Ages|What happens as materials degrade and records are lost?|Use dated inventory and condition records.
ethical_dilemma|Restore or Preserve Wear?|Does repair erase evidence of use or prevent loss?|State treatment alternatives and owner goals.
field_space_constraints|Storage for a Collection|How do size, access, and environmental needs shape shelving?|Measure actual objects and room.
field_household_cost|Full Collecting Cost|What purchase, shipping, insurance, and storage costs accrue?|Use dated itemized examples, not projected returns.
field_design_for_access|Who Can View It?|How can labels, placement, and digital records broaden access?|Test with intended visitors.
field_maintenance_burden|Condition Monitoring|Which cleaning, battery removal, and inspection tasks continue?|Use material-specific conservation advice.
field_material_lifecycle|Preserving versus Replacing|What materials and waste arise from storage and restoration?|Define boundary and treatment evidence.
"""

MODEL_BUILDING = """history_origins|A Scale-Model Practice|Which dated workshop or kit documents a modeling technique?|Identify subject, scale, maker, and purpose.
famous_examples|A Model beside Its Source|Which features of a named model match or simplify the original?|Compare verified source measurements and model.
hidden_stories|Makers of the Model|Who researched, drafted, fabricated, painted, and displayed it?|Check workshop and collection records.
beginner_explainers|What Scale Means|How do model and original dimensions relate?|State ratio, units, and a measured example.
advanced_concepts|Accuracy versus Readability|When does a scaled detail need exaggeration to be visible?|Compare viewing distance, medium, and design aim.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Unknown Model Prototype|Which features and provenance support a claimed subject?|Compare archival drawings and object evidence.
technology_innovation|Digital Tools in Modeling|What changed with scanning, cutting, or printing for one build?|Compare tolerances, cost, and manual finishing.
people_personalities|A Model Maker's Revision|Why did a builder alter a form or finish?|Use versioned plans and attributed notes.
major_events|A Model Enters an Exhibit|What changed in interpretation after public display?|Compare label, mounting, and visitor feedback.
how_it_works|From Reference to Model|How do source research, scaling, pattern, assembly, and finish connect?|Trace a documented build.
rise_fall|A Kit Reissued|Which tooling or historical reference changed between versions?|Compare dated kits and catalogs.
then_vs_now|A Model after Conservation|Which parts were original, repaired, or replaced?|Use condition and treatment records.
future_developments|A Planned Model Build|Which sources and materials are still needed to complete it?|State research gaps and constraints.
myths_vs_facts|A Model Is Exact?|Which shapes or mechanisms were simplified?|Compare ratio and documented compromises.
documentary_stories|Making a Scale Model|How did a project move from source plans to display?|Follow dated sketches, builds, and credits.
creative_brief|The Model's Purpose|Is it for testing, teaching, display, or play?|Match detail and durability to stated use.
materials_and_tools|Choosing Model Materials|How do wood, plastic, metal, or paper affect form and conservation?|Compare actual samples and tool limits.
process_breakdown|A Model Fit Test|Which measured mismatch prompted a revised part?|Use dimensioned plans and assembly notes.
composition_choice|What the Model Emphasizes|How do color, cutaway, and scale direct attention?|Compare model with source and intended audience.
collaborative_authorship|The Model Team|Who supplied source research, fabrication, painting, and display?|Attribute roles from records.
adaptation_across_media|Blueprint to Three Dimensions|Which 2D ambiguities needed interpretation during building?|Compare drawings with finished form.
audience_reception|Visitors Read a Model|Which features do viewers actually notice or misunderstand?|Use bounded exhibit observation.
cultural_context|A Model of Someone's Place|How are local knowledge and ownership represented?|Consult source communities and credit them.
preservation_restoration|Keeping a Model Intact|Which adhesives, paint, or supports are deteriorating?|Use conservation condition report.
rights_and_attribution|Plans and Kit Parts|Which drawings, logos, or designs require reuse permission?|Check source and model-maker credits.
style_comparison|Two Models, One Subject|How do scale and purpose alter detail?|Compare matched source evidence and display setting.
creative_failure|A Model Part Rebuilt|What material or measurement issue caused rework?|Use workshop and test records.
field_material_selection|Material for Fine Detail|Which strength, workability, and finish fit the model's scale?|Test samples and intended handling.
field_tool_control|Safe Detail Work|Which cutting, painting, and ventilation controls apply?|Use tool and material instructions, especially for child participation.
field_pattern_design|Scaling a Template|Which dimensions and tolerances must be transformed?|Show ratio and check fit against source.
field_repairability|Replaceable Components|Can damaged parts be removed without harming the whole?|Document joins and spare-part provenance.
field_craft_lineage|Model-Making Traditions|Which workshop or kit practices inform a named build?|Use dated examples and maker credit.
"""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("408", "408_toys", TOYS,
                  "Toys as designed play objects whose age suitability, material safety, child-led use, learning claims, household context, and version history need separate evidence.",
                  "identified product versions, manufacturer and test records, current CPSC safety and recall information, museum toy collections, and consented age-specific play observation",
                  "Name toy version, child age, setting, date, and jurisdiction. Do not certify safety from appearance or promise a developmental benefit from marketing or one play session.")
    revise_domain("409", "409_toy_collecting", COLLECTING,
                  "Toy collecting as the identification, provenance, care, display, exchange, and lived practice of keeping play objects over time.",
                  "object markings and packaging, dated catalogs, accession and ownership records, condition reports, completed sale data where relevant, and consented collector accounts",
                  "Separate historical value, personal value, and market price. Mark provenance gaps, verify recalls before reuse, and avoid investment advice.")
    revise_domain("410", "410_model_building", MODEL_BUILDING,
                  "Model building as scaled representation and craft shaped by reference evidence, material, fabrication, intended use, authorship, and conservation.",
                  "dimensioned source plans, model and kit versions, workshop notes, maker credits, museum model collections, condition reports, and bounded visitor studies",
                  "Name subject, scale, model version, and purpose. Distinguish a model's deliberate simplification from errors and check tool and material safety for the actual setting.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
